   "p": "There's no word for “of” or “'s”. Two nouns sit side by side, and their endings do the work:"
  },
  {
   "rule": "<strong>Iḍāfa</strong>: the first noun (the thing owned) has <strong>no tanwīn and no <span class='ar'>الْ</span></strong>: <span class='ar'>كِتَابُ</span>. The second noun (the owner) is <strong>majrūr</strong>, ending in kasra: <span class='ar jarr'>مُحَمَّدٍ</span>, <span class='ar jarr'>الْبَيْتِ</span>. The first noun becomes definite through the second: <span class='ar'>كِتَابُ مُحَمَّدٍ</span> = <em>the</em> book of Muhammad."
  },
